    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d288-a1">

                <pb facs="0773" n="651" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg651"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 7.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gomez to Mr. Loring.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-08-07"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 7,
                        1889</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Upon the subject of the note which Mr. Lewis did me the honor to address to me on
                    February 28 last past, I have the satisfaction to communicate to your excellency
                    that the fine imposed upon the captain of the American bark <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Carrie Heckle</hi> has been remitted, and there will be
                    returned to Mr. Colcord, or to his representative, the sum of 40,000 reis—amount
                    of that fine.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Barros Gomez.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
